const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'How long does shipping from China to France take?',
    a: 'WorldFreightHub Europe route data records roughly 30 days by sea from Shanghai, Ningbo-Zhoushan or Shenzhen to Le Havre on the current Cape-of-Good-Hope routing, with the Red Sea reroute adding about +10–14 days versus the pre-crisis Suez routing (MEDIUM confidence, because these are planning estimates, not carrier promises). Rail from Xi\u2019an or Chengdu into Europe runs roughly 18–22 days, but the final leg into France adds connection time. No verified France air transit is published in the snapshot — request that from your carrier rather than assuming the sea figure applies.',
